warm, it pushes blood away
from the outside of your body

00:08:33.203 --> 00:08:35.276
and pushes to the inside of your body--

00:08:35.276 --> 00:08:36.109
- Okay.

00:08:36.109 --> 00:08:38.450
- To keep your organs warm.
But when it does that, it

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:40.722
pushes the blood away from
the nose and away from the

00:08:40.722 --> 00:08:43.139
mouth. And it pushes away,
also all the white blood cells

00:08:43.139 --> 00:08:46.564
that protect your body from
infection. Plus the air is

00:08:46.564 --> 00:08:50.560
drier in the winter, so
viruses hang around more in the

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:53.330
air, people spend more time
inside during the winter--

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:54.163
- Right.

00:08:54.163 --> 00:08:55.176
- Because it's cold outside,
so they're in closer

00:08:55.176 --> 00:08:56.667
proximity, so you share all the viruses--

00:08:56.667 --> 00:08:57.500
- Oh.

00:08:57.500 --> 00:09:00.490
- So it's all those things,
people do get more sick when

00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:02.009
they travel, but--

00:09:02.009 --> 00:09:04.230
- Yeah, I just did Australia,
so it was like a 20 hour

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:05.063
flight--

00:09:05.063 --> 00:09:07.060
- Yeah, I just did a
China 20 hour flight--

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:08.560
- Yeah, I got sick after that flight.

